# Hexo Blog Post Guide

## Post Format
Blog posts use Markdown with YAML front matter at the top.

### Essential Front Matter
```yaml
---
title: Your Post Title
date: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
categories: 
  - Category1
  - Category2
tags:
  - Tag1
  - Tag2
---
```

### Publication Date Requirement
When creating a new post, the publication date (`date` field in front matter) must be set to the current network time rather than local system time to ensure consistency across all posts.

You can get the current network time using online services or the MCP time tool:
```
// Use MCP time tool to get accurate network time
mcp_time-mcp_current_time format="YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss"
```

### Optional Front Matter
```yaml
---
updated: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
description: Short description of the post
permalink: custom-url
thumbnail: path/to/image.jpg
pin: true  # Pin post to top of index
---
```

## Manual Post Creation
Since we're using GitHub Actions for deployment and don't need to run local Hexo commands:

1. Create a new Markdown file manually in the `source/_posts/` directory
2. File should be named: `YYYY-MM-DD-post-title.md` or similar format
3. Include proper front matter at the top
4. Write your content in Markdown format
5. Commit and push to GitHub to trigger the deployment

GitHub Actions will handle the Hexo commands (generate, deploy) on the server side.
